lsquare for Python includes code adapted from AgentCat's TypeScript SDK (the npm package
agentcat, version 2.1.0), by way of LSquare's own TypeScript SDK, which ports it. It is under the
MIT licence below: recognising an MCP server by its shape; the hook points (the request handler
map, re-arming when handlers are set again, tools registered late, the tap on each tool's own
function); reading the client's info; detecting multi-round calls; and adding the extras' inputs to
listed tools and removing them from calls. The files that hold it say so in a header.

